                                "sense_id": "5926db9a-1e02-3e3d-89e4-f841033cc68f",
                                "text": "The capital cost in 1915-1927 of equipping 924 miles of track put the Milwaukee into a receivership from which it took a long time to recover; and in view of the length of line electrified it is surprising that a current of 1,500V d.c. was chosen rather than the Pennsylvania 11,000V a.c."
                            }
                        ]
